## Engineering update

The course desk update says #4471 closed on 5 October 2026. Engineering marked the parser **fixed** with `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. It marked the form hint **won't fix** because `booking-v3` was retired. These are different outcomes for two problems that shared one support ticket.

## Parser reads month first

The shared parser reads numeric dates month first even when the tenant writes the day first. An ambiguous date can move to another month. In report R-41200, a 7 April reminder became 4 July. This cause spans app, email, and some form reports. The [parser issue](https://github.com/jasonhardy/mega_dev_w1c3/issues/1) tracks the fix.

## Form hint disagrees with form parsing

For day-first tenants on `booking-v3`, the form shows `MM/DD/YYYY` while interpreting the entry by the tenant's day-first convention. The person follows the hint and gets another date. In R-41230, 6 January became 1 June. This cause is specific to the form path. The [form hint issue](https://github.com/jasonhardy/mega_dev_w1c3/issues/2) tracks it separately.

## How the counts were made

The ticket export has overlapping pages, so one report ID counts once. We include only reports merged into #4471, then use each tenant's locale and booking form with the channel to assign a cause, as implemented in `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`. Intake tags describe the first guess, not the cause. The five reports in `desk-notes.json` read as one-day moves are counted under the parser cause by tenant and remain flagged for follow-up; this export does not establish a separate root cause for them.

The accepted [subject-line dedupe decision](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) and [triage guide](/kb/triage/dedupe) can merge different causes. This case shows why the desk should inspect report bodies, tenant locale, form version, and channel before treating a merged ticket as one fix. The old decision record stays as accepted history.

